    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9321" root="حنط" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَّاطٌ</span></b>  <i>A seller of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِنْطَة</span> [or <i>wheat</i>]; (S, Mgh,
Msb, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَّاطِىٌّ</span></b> ; (K;) a rel. n. from the
former. (Msb.) [The pl.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَّاطُونَ</span> is explained
by the lawyers as signifying <i>Persons who transport wheat</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِنْطَة</span>) <i>from the ship to the houses.</i>
(Mgh in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نقل</span>.)

